  "domain": "security",
  "definition": "Asymmetric Cryptography is a cryptographic paradigm in which mathematically related key pairs \u2014 a public key and a private key \u2014 serve distinct roles: the public key may be freely shared and used to encrypt messages or verify signatures, while the private key is kept secret and used to decrypt or sign. Security rests on the computational intractability of reversing the underlying mathematical problems without knowledge of the private key.",
